		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Réponse à&#160;:  [RESOLU] [PAF] changement du port par défaut 5432]]></title>
		<link rel="alternate" href="http://forums.postgresql.fr/viewtopic.php?pid=25583#p25583"/>
		<content type="html"><![CDATA[<p>Si on prend le tuto, ça veut juste rajouter un paramètre pgport. Au lieu de</p><div class="codebox"><pre><code># 1. resource pgsqld
primitive pgsqld pgsqlms                                                      \
  params pgdata=&quot;/var/lib/postgresql/9.6/main&quot;                                \
         bindir=&quot;/usr/lib/postgresql/9.6/bin&quot;                                 \
         pghost=&quot;/var/run/postgresql&quot;                                         \
         recovery_template=&quot;/etc/postgresql/9.6/main/recovery.conf.pcmk&quot;      \
         start_opts=&quot;-c config_file=/etc/postgresql/9.6/main/postgresql.conf&quot; \
  op start timeout=60s                                                        \
  op stop timeout=60s                                                         \
  op promote timeout=30s                                                      \
  op demote timeout=120s                                                      \
  op monitor interval=15s timeout=10s role=&quot;Master&quot;                           \
  op monitor interval=16s timeout=10s role=&quot;Slave&quot;                            \
  op notify timeout=60s</code></pre></div><p>On mettrait</p><div class="codebox"><pre><code># 1. resource pgsqld
primitive pgsqld pgsqlms                                                      \
  params pgdata=&quot;/var/lib/postgresql/9.6/main&quot;                                \
         bindir=&quot;/usr/lib/postgresql/9.6/bin&quot;                                 \
         pghost=&quot;/var/run/postgresql&quot;                                         \
         pgport=&quot;6432&quot;                                         \
         recovery_template=&quot;/etc/postgresql/9.6/main/recovery.conf.pcmk&quot;      \
         start_opts=&quot;-c config_file=/etc/postgresql/9.6/main/postgresql.conf&quot; \
  op start timeout=60s                                                        \
  op stop timeout=60s                                                         \
  op promote timeout=30s                                                      \
  op demote timeout=120s                                                      \
  op monitor interval=15s timeout=10s role=&quot;Master&quot;                           \
  op monitor interval=16s timeout=10s role=&quot;Slave&quot;                            \
  op notify timeout=60s</code></pre></div><p>par exemple (pour reprendre l&#039;exemple du tuto de PAF)</p>]]></content>
